<title>UK: Group to announce UK military homes sale - paper.</title>
<headline>Group to announce UK military homes sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Annington Homes, the group backed by Japan's Nomura Securities Co Ltd which took over the married quarters of Britain's armed forces last year, is to announce the sale of 203 of the homes on Monday, The Times newspaper said.</p>
<p>The report said the sale will bring to 330 the total number of homes sold, making up nearly 15 percent of the &quot;surplus estate&quot; that it took over under last year's 1.66 billion pounds sale.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
